            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0250" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 16—7:22 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>449. Following from Smyrna: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 13, noon. I have just had notification from the Greek High
                            Commission that the treaty clauses<anchor n="12" xml:id="d135-f1"/> will
                            be carried out as from yesterday; that the Ottoman officials are
                            superseded by Greek authorities; that the transfer of government
                            commenced yesterday and that relations between the new authorities and
                            foreign representatives will be carried out through the Greek High
                            Commission. Government building, Custom House and <hi
                                rendition="#italic">gendarme</hi> stations were taken last night
                            without opposition and Ottoman officials superseded. Despatch will be
                            forwarded. Russell.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
